      In this context, \env{ansitermexec} allows (when @1 is enabled) the execution and logging of shell commands and their results, with ANSI control characters being correctly interpreted.
      If @2 is set, the output is tagged.

      This package is part of the \pkg*{osglecture} bundle, but is largely
      independent of the other packages.
